From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:37:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Give each compute unit its own UMA
 pool again by default

Since "Share one UMA pool between a VM's compute units by default" every
compute unit of a VM allocates from unit 0's page ring, while each unit
keeps its own allocator descriptor. The firmware loads the ring indices
from a command's descriptor when it binds the command and saves them back
when it retires it, and a reused unit gets its old descriptor back. With
several commands in flight the descriptors disagree about which pages are
free, and a page can be handed to two work groups that run at the same
time.

The concurrent render and compute stress test shows it: about once per
thousand copies a 1024x1024 image-to-buffer copy loses a few stores of
one or two work groups, or stores another work group's texel, on every
seed. 1.1007, which had one pool per unit, passes 3 of 3 seeds with
44,000 checks each. With g16_compute_shared_pool=0 this tree passes 3 of
3 seeds with 93,000 checks each and no GPU fault.

Go back to one 32 MiB pool per unit. g16_compute_shared_pool=1 keeps the
shared pool available until it has one descriptor per VM, as macOS has.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 6580b7aaf8..e584786c5c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -854,8 +854,8 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_units() -> usize {
     "G16: compute units per VM, one compute command in flight each (default 16; 2..16; 12 = k948; 8 = before; 4 = k908; 9..16 = deeper compute queue, ~33 MiB per unit, 13..16 for g16_horizon up to 15; latched at the engine start, set it as a module option)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_shared_pool` (0644, default 1; latched at its first read).
-static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_shared_pool` (0644, default 0; latched at its first read).
+static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
 /// 0 until latched, then 1 (off) or 2 (on).
 static COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL_LATCH: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
 
@@ -889,7 +889,7 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_shared_pool_state() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL_PARM,
     COMPUTE_SHARED_POOL,
     "g16_compute_shared_pool",
-    "G16: 1 (default) = all compute units of a VM allocate from unit 0's UMA pool, each command keeping its own descriptor, UMA slot and context store; 0 = one 32 MiB pool per unit; latched at the first compute command, set it as a module option"
+    "G16: 1 = all compute units of a VM allocate from unit 0's UMA pool, each command keeping its own descriptor, UMA slot and context store; 0 (default) = one 32 MiB pool per unit; latched at the first compute command, set it as a module option"
 );
 
 live_u32_param!(
